[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   step_119: Mechanism identification for the post-2017 displaced dipole.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   Step 118 established that the prospective cohort's discrepancy field
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   carries a coherent, cohort-private dipole -- unipolar (cos1 dominant),
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   displaced ~80-120 deg off the declared axis, organised primarily in
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   aphelion ecliptic longitude (phase ~182 deg), invisible to the CODE
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   cohort at the same sky position, and strongest in the shorter-arc
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   half of the sample.  The manuscript reads it as a longitude-organised
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   systematic of the post-2017 orbit solutions and states its origin is
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   identifiable in principle.  This step performs the identification:
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   every computable observing-geometry and fit-record covariate is scored
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   against the residual field, and the dipole is re-measured after each
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   covariate is absorbed into the baseline regression.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   Hypotheses under test
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   H-GEO   opposition/elongation geometry: short-arc orbits observed
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   near solar conjunction carry a line-of-sight degeneracy that
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   inflates the boundary-reconstruction discrepancy; the dipole
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   longitude then reflects where the perihelion sat relative to
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   Earth at mid-arc, not an inertial direction.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   H-WEAK  weak-direction projection: the aphelion direction of a
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   short-arc solution errs along the geocentric observing
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   direction; resid should grow as |u_aph . g_hat| -> 1.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   H-ARC   arc asymmetry: arcs that do not span perihelion (all-pre or
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   all-post) produce systematically different solutions than
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   spanning arcs.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   H-SURV  survey lineage: a single survey's fit record carries the
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   dipole; within-survey subsets are clean.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   H-YEAR  designation-year composition: the dipole is carried by one
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   discovery season.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   H-RES   none of the measured covariates absorbs the dipole -- it is
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   a structural property of the modern fit record not reducible
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   to observing geometry (e.g. a pipeline-level systematic in
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   epoch/NG handling).
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   Tests
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   T1  Spearman correlations: resid and raw drot against every
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   covariate (opposition factor, elongation, geocentric distance,
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   weak-direction cosine, pre-perihelion arc fraction, days from
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   perihelion at mid-arc, arc, nobs, q, i, e, cc, year).
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   T2  absorption: the recovered-axis cap-gap re-measured with each
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   covariate appended to the step_063 residual regression -- which
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   covariate(s) shrink the dipole.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   T3  joint harmonic + covariate fit: the order-1 longitude amplitude
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   before and after all geometry covariates are entered together.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   T4  survey stratification and leave-one-survey-out.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   T5  leave-one-year-out on designation year.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   T6  sample splits: deep-plunger vs extended, bound vs hyperbolic,
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   near-perihelion-observed vs distant-arc.
[2026-10-16 13:43:31 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 119]   Inputs
